ai_context: >-
  Benchmark evidence database for the omni-benchmark LiveSQLBench evaluation.
  Grain: one attempt per row in neondb_telemetry__attempt, keyed by attempt_id
  and generation_record_sha256. Use arm (C1, C2, C3, C4, C5, E02) as the
  analysis unit; condition is the preregistered condition and stores C5 and
  E02 as C4. Correctness exists only for partition dev-a, in
  neondb_telemetry__score, with two frozen scorers that are always reported
  together: official_soft_ex (benchmark-comparable) and sensitivity. Accuracy
  is correct divided by status = scored rows of that scorer. Sealed test
  attempts (partition test) carry telemetry only; their published rates live
  in neondb_telemetry__sealed_aggregate. Prefer the modeled measures over
  reconstructing them. Cross-arm accuracy comparisons must be filtered to
  neondb_telemetry__dev_a_frame.in_official_frame (122 questions) or
  in_sensitivity_frame (121 questions); unfiltered per-arm denominators are
  not comparable because the arms did not all run the same questions. Cost is
  unavailable by construction for C4, C5 and E02 and must never be estimated
  from token counts.
